# nr-office-ooxml-pptx-deck: integration fragment

Three modules and one test join the crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml): pptx_deck (the deck operations of
portable-pptx-deck.mjs: add, delete, move, keep, duplicate and import slides, comments, provenance, notes, template tokens,
text replacement, background, footer, page number, theme, layout, visibility, transition), pptx_table_fit
(pptx-table-fit.mjs) and snapshot_pptx (portable-snapshot-pptx.mjs). No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name
belongs to them; nothing registers them. The later task nr-office-ooxml-pptx-charts (the pptx dispatcher) calls the handlers.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After the line `pub mod pptx_core;` (modules are in the order the file lists them), add:

    pub mod pptx_deck;

After `pub mod pptx_targets;` add:

    pub mod pptx_table_fit;

After `pub mod snapshot_shared;` add:

    pub mod snapshot_pptx;

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/Cargo.toml

pptx_deck.rs writes the id of a page-number field as a version 4 UUID (Node's randomUUID). In [dependencies], after the line
`tokio = { workspace = true, features = ["rt", "time", "net", "process", "io-util"] }`, add:

    uuid = { workspace = true, features = ["v4"] }

The workspace entry `uuid = "1"` and the Cargo.lock package already exist (mixdog-connections and others use the v4
feature), so no new crate is needed and mixdog-workspace-hack needs no new feature.

## native/core/Cargo.lock

In the package entry of mixdog-ooxml, add "uuid" to its dependencies (between "tokio" and "zip", in the order the lock sorts
them).

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-pptx-base (keep the list sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-deck.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-pptx-deck/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "2d0f6752f38a5ded03986a6dd6e645df0678eca6dfe8f00011b0d69db0be800a",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-deck.mjs",
      "set": "office-pptx-deck",
      "totalBytes": 753836
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-pptx-deck/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool that
keeps this file reorders or reformats them.)

## What the pptx dispatcher (nr-office-ooxml-pptx-charts) calls

Every handler takes the package, the slide roster the batch keeps (`&mut Vec<SlideRef>` where Node's handler reassigns
`context.slides`, `&[SlideRef]` where it does not), and the operation as a serde_json Value; it answers the Value Node's
handler returned or the message Node threw. import_slides and apply_theme read a file and take a `ReadProof` first:

    handle_add_slide, handle_delete_slide, handle_move_slide, handle_keep_slides, handle_duplicate_slide(zip, &mut slides, op)
    handle_import_slides(proof, zip, &mut slides, op)
    handle_add_comment_or_delete_comment (add_comment, delete_comment), handle_add_provenance, handle_set_notes,
    handle_replace_text, handle_set_slide_background, handle_set_footer_or_set_slide_number (set_footer, set_slide_number),
    handle_set_layout, handle_set_slide_visibility, handle_set_transition(zip, &slides, op)
    handle_fill_template(zip, op), handle_apply_theme(proof, zip, op)

snapshot_pptx::snapshot_pptx(zip, options, &TextMeasurer) answers the snapshot JSON; the measurer is the one the table
heights are measured with (a table is drawn as tall as its rows' text needs, so it needs the faces).

## Not compiled

The three modules and the test were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead). The first build of
mixdog-ooxml and its tests, cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml, is the check. The twin test tests/twin_pptx_deck.rs replays
native/core/fixtures/office-pptx-deck and needs no Node, but registers the fixture face native/core/fixtures/office-measure/
faces/MiriamLibre-Regular.otf for the table measurements; twin_live_pptx_deck (ignored) re-records through Node.
